Z||000001||Lynx||06-04-99||12:39 AM||||Dont know how to fix it try looking at a wiring diagram in a chilton manual to pin point the problem. Well i have a friend that has a problem with that on his car he just rigged a switch.
Z||000002||theogre||06-04-99||07:04 AM||||there is a relay, and a switch, in that curcuit. One of them has failed. The relay is usually in the vapor canister area. the switch is screwed into an oil gallery in the block.<p>unplug the relay, if it stops it's the relay. if it doesn't it's the oil presure switch.
